title: The Soldiers
subtitle: The Reichswehr has orders to fire. Not every soldier will.
view-if: crisis_october = 1 and e23_rising_phase = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.octTick(Q.crisis_time + 1);
Q.e23_officers_ok = 0;
!}
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Soldiers

Seeckt's officers are monarchists. His soldiers are mostly the sons of farmers and craftsmen, paid in the same marks as everyone else. The Prussian police are run by Social Democrats, and half the constables in Berlin carry an SPD card.

- @leaflets: Flood the barracks with leaflets.
- @officers: Buy the officers who hate Seeckt.
- @police: Talk to the police through their union.

@leaflets
subtitle: Cheap. Some soldiers will read them.
on-arrival: {!
Q.army_loyalty -= 4;
Q.repression += 2;
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

The leaflet is four lines long and addressed to the soldier's mother. One is found in every locker of a battalion in Dresden, and the sentries are doubled.

@officers
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The apparatus gives it two chances in five.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e23_officers_ok = Math.random() < 0.4 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e23_officers_ok) {
    Q.army_loyalty -= 9;
    Q.e23_oct_bonus += 2;
} else {
    Q.e23_oct_bonus -= 1;
    Q.independence -= 2;
}
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

[? if e23_officers_ok = 1 : A captain at Döberitz and a major in Leipzig promise that their companies will stay in barracks. On the second day they keep their word. ?][? if e23_officers_ok = 0 : The officers take the money and pass our names to Seeckt's intelligence office. ?]

@police
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] They will not rise. They might not shoot.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('united_front');
Q.police_loyalty -= 6;
Q.e23_oct_bonus += Q.spd_relation >= 35 ? 2 : 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
RG.e22.octLines();
!}

Two delegates of the police union meet our people in a back room in Leipzig. They will not join anything. They say that their men will not fire on a picket line.
